  {
    "udt_union_v0": {
      "doc": "Sentinel for an amount slot of a command argument.\\n\\n`Balance` instructs the dispatcher to use the Router's current balance\\nof the relevant token (Solidity's `CONTRACT_BALANCE` sentinel). `Exact`\\nis a plain `i128` value.\\n\\nNOTE: `TransferFrom + Balance` is a special case \\xe2\\x80\\x94 the owner is the\\ncaller, so it resolves to `token.balance(&caller)` and attempts to pull\\nthat entire balance via SEP-41 `transfer_from`. The caller must have\\npre-approved the Router for at least that amount, otherwise the call\\npanics with `InsufficientAllowance`. All other commands resolve\\n`Balance` against the Router's own balance.",
      "lib": "",
      "name": "Amount",
      "cases": [
        {
          "void_v0": {
            "doc": "",
            "name": "Balance"
          }
        },
        {
          "tuple_v0": {
            "doc": "",
            "name": "Exact",
            "type_": [
              "i128"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "udt_union_v0": {
      "doc": "The Router's `execute(caller, commands, deadline)` entry point loops\\nover a `Vec<Command>` and dispatches each variant. Sentinel enums in\\nthe recipient/amount slots are resolved per command.\\n\\nVariants map to Solidity opcodes from `Commands.sol`:\\n- `TransferFrom`             \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x00 TRANSFER_FROM\\n- `Transfer`                 \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x02 TRANSFER\\n- `AssertMinBalance`         \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x0f ASSERT_MIN_BALANCE\\n- `DepositAssetInIbt`        \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x04 DEPOSIT_ASSET_IN_IBT\\n- `DepositIbtInPt`           \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x06 DEPOSIT_IBT_IN_PT\\n- `RedeemIbtForAsset`        \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x07 REDEEM_IBT_FOR_ASSET\\n- `RedeemPtForIbt`           \\xe2\\x86\\x92 0x09 REDEEM_PT_FOR_IBT\\n- `CancelOrders`             \\xe2\\x86\\x92 (Stellar-only; no Solidity opcode)\\n- `FillOrders`               \\xe2\\x86\\x92 (Stellar-only; no Solidity opcode)\\n- `BridgeNativePtToEvm`      \\xe2\\x86\\x92 (Stellar-only; no Solidity opcode)\\n- `BridgeWrappedPtBackToEvm` \\xe2\\x86\\x92 (Stellar-only; no Solidity opcode)\\n- `BrokerSwap`               \\xe2\\x86\\x92 (Stellar-only; no Solidity opcode)",
      "lib": "",
      "name": "Command",
      "cases": [
        {
          "tuple_v0": {
            "doc": "",
            "name": "TransferFrom",
            "type_": [
              {
                "udt": {
                  "name": "TransferFromArgs"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "tuple_v0": {
            "doc": "",
            "name": "Transfer",
            "type_": [
